    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You’ve probably noticed something about the car industry over the last few years. Or rather, the lack of something. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " have disappeared from many cars. Touch screens have "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " instead. From turning on the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "wipers",
            "zh": "雨刮器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to turning down the heat, all you do is tap a screen."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The trend largely started with Tesla cars. They are "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for their clean and simple "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "interiors",
            "zh": "内饰"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The company’s newest cars don’t even have a traditional "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "shifter",
            "zh": "换挡装置"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". If you want the car to start moving forward, use the touchscreen to put it into "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Touchscreens are very common in new cars. According to a recent survey, nearly all (97%) of new cars "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " after 2023 have at least one touchscreen. About 25% of US cars on the road have a screen at least 11 inches long."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There are many reasons for carmakers’ "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for touch screens. For one thing, they can "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " money and production time by putting as few "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "wires",
            "zh": "电线"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " as possible through the car. Locating most "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "functions",
            "ref": "v-function"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on a touchscreen also allows them to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " functions over the air. With such screens, carmakers could even make money from advertising."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But using a screen while driving takes eyes "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and that can be very dangerous. Looking away from the road for two or more seconds doubles the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "likelihood",
            "ref": "v-likelihood"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of a(n) "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". According to a 2017 study, drivers were "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "distracted",
            "ref": "v-distracted"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for about 40 seconds while using touchscreens. US traffic "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "authorities",
            "ref": "v-authority"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " said 8% of all US traffic deaths in 2021 resulted from "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b11",
            "number": 11
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " drivers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Europe’s New Car Assessment Program (Euro NCAP) provides the public with information on the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b12",
            "number": 12
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of new cars. It tests cars and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "assigns",
            "ref": "v-assign"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " them safety ratings on a five-star "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scale",
            "ref": "v-scale"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This March, the agency published new testing rules. Under the new rules, a car won’t earn top scores "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b13",
            "number": 13
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " certain basic functions have their own buttons. The new rules will go "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "into effect",
            "zh": "生效"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in 2026."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Euro NCAP doesn’t have the authority to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b14",
            "number": 14
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " carmakers to use buttons. But it will give no more than 4 stars to cars that rely "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b15",
            "number": 15
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on touchscreens. Will that help stop a complete move away from buttons in cars? We have yet to find out."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
